            <ArticleTitle>[Diabetes and cardiovascular diseases in old age].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>172-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00391-011-0216-z</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The treatment of cardiovascular diseases in diabetic geriatric patients needs an individual risk-benefit analysis. The overtreatment of hyperglycemia in the sense of metabolic control that is too tight (HbA(1)c level &lt;6%) may lead to increased mortality. As a rule, the target HbA(1)c level in geriatric patients with diabetes mellitus should be between 7 and 8%.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
